    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0118" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14503/28.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Sherrill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 98.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your information before the arrival of
                    the first fleet at Buenos Aires, I inclose herewith a copy of a letter from the
                    Secretary of the Navy, stating that the squadron, which will be commanded by
                    Rear Admiral Staunton, will be known as the United States Special Service
                    Squadron, specifying the vessels which will compose the squadron, and
                    transmitting a list<anchor n="1" xml:id="d7-f1"/> of the commissioned and
                    warrant officers of each ship.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d7-a1.xml" xpointer="d7-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
